{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138133-iremite-soldiers","id":138133,"title":"Iremite Soldiers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-15T09:21:00-07:00","id":138133,"title":"Iremite Soldiers","content":"Why is it that there is no military faction among the Deathless? You'd think that someone among the Shan'iatu would have wanted soldiers in the ranks of ever-living servants, so what gives?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:54:26-07:00","id":138163,"title":"","content":"Makes you wonder, doesn't it? For some reason, the Shan'iatu chose to give their slave drivers, money changers, scribes, priests and architects immortality, but they picked not one person with military training to join the ranks of the immortal. Surely there must be some reason for that decision of theirs.<br /> <br /> Unless, of course, the soldiers are the sixth guild. Or the seventh. It's not like any of the Arisen really, truly remember anything meaningful about Irem, with the possible exception of one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":286,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","user":"Christian A","date":". 05-15-2014, 12:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T09:57:38-07:00","id":138166,"title":"","content":"What would be the utility of keeping your army around after the empire the army served no longer existed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T12:58:14-07:00","id":138341,"title":"","content":"If I remember correctly Guildhalls talks about this issue a bit.<br /> <br /> Basically, Irem's army was made up of a lot of smaller military groups. Each Shan'Iatu, the Pharaoh and each noble house all had &quot;house guards&quot; and malitia and such. When Irem went to war or conquest these were arranged under generals and whichever Shan'Iatu were involved with the military action. <br /> <br /> So I think it comes down to simple logistics. There was no &quot;soldier guild&quot; in the same way that their were the 5 (actually 6) major craft guilds. <br /> <br /> Soldiers may have been seen as a particular sort of laborer or class, butting them in a similar social position to the Guildmembers. Alternatively they might have been mainly drawn from slave stock and as such the majority of the military would have been even lower class then the &quot;middlish&quot; Guildmembers. Some fluff mentions general that seem to have been nobles, so its possible that the military may have been a very encompassing cross-class institution. More likely each Shan'Iatu, noble or the Pharaoh decided on what composition their armed forces was made up of. <br /> <br /> Another point to highlight is that the Guilds correspond to the 5 relic types. Each guild has a particular relation with a certain type of relic. We know the Judges demand relics delivered back to them in Duat above pretty much everything else. Its the Arisen's main purpose. <br /> <br /> Since soldiers would not have corresponded to a relic type (though I imagine they may have used them in Irem) they would have been far less effective at tracking them down. So it was not worth the &quot;investment&quot; of enacting the Rite of Return on them for the &quot;returns&quot; that such Arisen might have yielded. <br /> <br /> Alternatively, to get more metaphysical, maybe the fact that Soldiers would not correspond to a major relic type meant that they simply could not return from Duat after the Rite of Return or that the Rite of Return simply could not be enacted on them? Its a bit of a stretch, but its a theory. <br /> <br /> To get more practical again, we could consider the decision to choose merchants, scribes/judges, laborers/middle management, priests and architects as somewhat telling about the Shan'Iatu's intentions. These are the trades that would allow for a the establishment of a functioning &quot;Arisen Society&quot; in a manner of speaking. <br /> <br /> Certainly these groups working in co-ordination seem cherry picked to help in the creation and formalization of mortal cults as a method of infrastructure and the survival (in a fashion) of classical Iremite mystical traditions (centered around the 5 relics) via modified Guild structure and tradition. All of which makes sure some mystical resonance of Irem survives down through the ages via symbolism, mystical traditions, religious beliefs and at least a limited amount of historical record, all of which seems to be keeping the Judges &quot;hooks in the world&quot; perhaps? <br /> <br /> Soldiers, with little to no understanding of the aspects of Iremite mysticism, crafts and magical practices (abate in a very stunted rote form) could not have served this purpose anymore then they would have been the optimum choice to locate relics. So I guess we could say there are a few possible and plausible reasons but no hard and fast reason has been given in the books as such. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138133-iremite-soldiers?p=138163#post138163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless, of course, the soldiers are the sixth guild. Or the seventh. It's not like any of the Arisen really, truly remember anything meaningful about Irem, with the possible exception of one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sixth guild are mentioned as &quot;Artists&quot;. We know they seem to have a great deal of knowledge regarding astronomy and that they practiced name magic and understood &quot;the Will&quot; of magic. I'm thinking they might have been less &quot;artists&quot; in the traditional sense and possible either a guild of outright magicians or possibly philosophers/academics in a very, very different way from the Scribes who were more tax records, the law and history then actual learning it seems. <br /> <br /> While the idea of a seventh or even more Guilds is an interest thought experiment out-of-game sources confirm that Irem only at 6 actual Guilds. Great idea for an alternate less &quot;fractured&quot; military structure then the one talked about in Guildhalls though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:33:46-07:00","id":138363,"title":"","content":"Spoiler territory, dude. This is not a thread for spoilers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T13:46:43-07:00","id":138373,"title":"","content":"No reason why one can't have a hidden Soldier guild as a plot point. Imagine how terrifying the wakened Mummies would be when they hear rumours of a great warrior awakening; one who had been a warrior in life! And if a single warrior (with appropriate combat-specs) makes a good plot point, than imagine what happens when they learn that there IS a guild of them, something that you can base on ideas of the Mithraic cult, a mystical cult in the real world that spread amongst Roman soldiers from Mesopotamia. Not familiar enough with Mummy to know whether weapons or armour are already under a type of relic, but I assume they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:41:00-07:00","id":138672,"title":"","content":"The way I handled it was sort of what had been mentioned above: the rank and file soldiers were slaves, while the officers between the shan'iatu and the soldiers were members of the guild of the shan'iatu controlling their Legion. Maa'kep would coordinate military action and help in supplying the front lines, often serving to spread irem's philosophy. Mesen-Nebu would be &quot;martial artists&quot; and weaponsmiths, warriors with alchemically enhanced weapons, etc. Sesha-hebsu would be warriors of law, on sight battle recorders, and perhaps blademasters with enscribed swords. su-Menent would be (un)holy warriors like the templar or crusaders, using dark mysteries and deathly knowledge to kill. Tef-aabhi would serve as military strategists, designing perfect battle and defensive formations, or mastering the heka of flesh and war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T17:44:50-07:00","id":138673,"title":"","content":"The Mummy core and Guildhalls make occasional references to &quot;slave armies&quot; and the like. The Maa-Kep were responsible for herding this soldiers into battle, but that was the extent of guild involvement. It suggests that soldiers were largely considered no more remarkable than the slaves who extracted minerals from mines and the like. Many of the Shuankhsen may have been soldiers in life, but that's not really a sign of power or status in ancient Irem.<br /> <br /> That said, Guildhalls says that there was a branch of the Su-Menent called the Shemsu, who were dedicated defenders of the temples. If you want a Mummy who was a fighter in life, a Shemsu would be the way to go. Alternatively, a Maa-Kep Flail Bearer (I think that's the term), who are generally summoned to deal with supernatural foes. I think they are implied to have often been the slave drivers who forces the armies of Irem into battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T18:58:25-07:00","id":138722,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Given what's been said, I suppose it's not a matter of there not being soldiers <i>per se</i>, but of there not being a proper Soldier's Guild, with militant Arisen holding specialist roles within select guilds.<br /> <br /> On a similar note, can anyone think of any other non-standard professions that fit into the Guilds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T20:58:32-07:00","id":138853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/138133-iremite-soldiers?p=138363#post138363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spoiler territory, dude. This is not a thread for spoilers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shkspr1048 asked a question. I provided an answer based on knowledge in Guildhalls and the Core that is certainly interesting and does reveal a little as to the social structure of Irem hardly a &quot;break the game spoiler&quot;. Likewise, the Sixth Guild stuff is nothing that is not in a player section. The guild limit of 6 is mentioned in multiple sidebars in various books in player areas. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-15T21:12:19-07:00","id":138875,"title":"","content":"I mean, historically, career soldiers and standing armies weren't really a widespread thing in that period. Using egyptian history as a marker, they didn't really start occurring until the new kingdom. Which is something like two or three millenia after Irem. Assuming they did it like Egypt did, it's possible that any member of any guild <i>fought in a war</i>, but they wouldn't identify as soldiers, because no one really did. Armies were assembled when you needed to <i>do something</i>, and then disbanded when the job was done.<br /> <br /> Think of it like the folks who got drafted into vietnam. They went to war, but they wouldn't summarize their lives as &quot;I was a soldier&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":996,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","user":"Gabby","date":". 05-16-2014, 12:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/996-gabby","name":"Gabby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T02:15:23-07:00","id":140355,"title":"","content":"Irem is an &quot;ur&quot; society, with no reason that they wouldn't have realized the value of a standing army, especially with their conquest oriented political system. Rome, while not Egypt, celebrated the conquering heroes and had a similar perspective as the Iremites, &quot;We are the greatest, and we will conquer all the world&quot;. Valuable soldiers may belong to other guilds, but if you want your artifacts and objects preserved, why not use someone who knows how to fight, to kill, and to protect?<br /> <br /> Some people do summarize themselves as Soldiers though, so it's just as valid as &quot;I was an artist&quot; or &quot;I kept the laws&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2861-nyx","name":"Nyx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2861_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T04:46:23-07:00","id":140423,"title":"","content":"Isn't it kind of the point that the Arisen weren't soldiers? They were upper class - middle class, in a way, but wealthy and prestigious; they were the intermediaries between the pharaoh/Shan'iatu and the common folk. It's their snobby attitude that's made enemies out of the Shuankhsen and Deceived. Not every splat has a 'fighter y-splat' anyway.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Although they were probably fighting for the Empire's enemies, there are no doubt Shuankhsen who were once soldiers</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}